{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And I turned again, flying</b> — as though it flies; therefore it is written: \"that goes out over the face of all the earth.\" Some say: כפולה [folded/doubled] is from the Aramaic root, but there is no sense to his interpretation. Yefet said: spread open, like \"and they flew on the shoulder of Philistia\" [Isaiah 11:14]."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:00.088763646Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}